&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Calibri'; font-size:16pt; color:#000000;&quot;&gt;Dynamic OCP Test&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Calibri'; font-size:11pt; color:#000000;&quot;&gt;1.) Do it on a real board. Use a DC power supply to power on the regulator instead of using AC adapter. You may need additional steps here to enable regulator&lt;br /&gt;2.) Add rework similar to Picture shared in rework tab. That can be used for most of the Power validation&lt;br /&gt;3.) Add rework to connect e-load to output of power rail preferably close to real sink&lt;br /&gt;4.) Probe Vout and Iout. Capture current when Vout goes down&lt;br /&gt;5.) Power on at noload and slowly increase the e-load until power rail shutsdown&lt;br /&gt;Purpose: Find OC suhtdown point&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Calibri'; font-size:16pt; color:#000000;&quot;&gt;Static OCP Test&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Calibri'; font-size:11pt; color:#000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;br /&gt;1.) Do it on a real board. Use a DC power supply to power on the regulator instead of using AC adapter. You may need additional steps here to enable regulator&lt;br /&gt;2.) Add rework similar to Picture shared in rework tab. That can be used for most of the Power validation&lt;br /&gt;3.) Add rework to connect e-load to output of power rail preferably close to real sink&lt;br /&gt;4.) Probe Vout and Iout. Capture current when Vout goes down&lt;br /&gt;5.) Setup e-load to the value where the rails shutdown during Dynamic OCP test&lt;br /&gt;6.) Power on the rail&lt;br /&gt;Purpose: Make sure board doesn't damage when turned on into over current&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Calibri'; font-size:16pt; color:#000000;&quot;&gt;Short Circuit Test&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Calibri'; font-size:11pt; color:#000000;&quot;&gt;1.) Do it on a real board. Use a DC power supply to power on the regulator instead of using AC adapter. You may need additional steps here to enable regulator&lt;br /&gt;2.) Add rework similar to Picture shared in rework tab. That can be used for most of the Power validation&lt;br /&gt;3.) Add rework to connect output to GND. Do rework to make sure you have enough current path to GND to avoid thermal events&lt;br /&gt;4.) Power on the rail&lt;br /&gt;Purpose: Make sure board doesn't damage when turned on into over current&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</string>
            </property>
           </widget>
          </widget>
         </widget>
        </widget>
