&lt;/style&gt;&lt;/head&gt;&lt;body style=&quot; font-family:'PMingLiU'; font-size:9pt; font-weight:400; font-style:normal;&quot;&gt;
&lt;table border=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px;&quot; width=&quot;659&quot; cellspacing=&quot;0&quot; cellpadding=&quot;0&quot;&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td width=&quot;659&quot; style=&quot; vertical-align:middle;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Calibri'; font-size:12pt; color:#000000;&quot;&gt;Test Procedure&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:12pt;&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td style=&quot; vertical-align:top;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Calibri'; font-size:12pt; color:#000000;&quot;&gt;Do this test after you know how to exercise each sub-system to their max capability&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;1.) Put device into stress mode, so it can draw max power&lt;br /&gt;2.) Use a precision multimeter and measure the voltage difference between Source and Sink (Multimeter Red at Source and Black at Sink1). Repeat at all sinks. &lt;br /&gt;3.) Worst case among all 3 is the worst DC Drop&lt;br /&gt;4.) Number of sinks depends on how the power planes are routed. Trying to measure at all corner locations&lt;br /&gt;Pass/Fail: +/-3%&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:12pt;&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</string>
